  "typical_application": "Analog/digital signal routing, multiplexing, sample-and-hold, channel mute/switching in audio and synth circuits. Control pin high closes the switch.",
  "gotchas": [
    "the analog signal must stay between VSS and VDD; for bipolar audio you need a dual supply (VSS negative) or to bias the signal mid-rail",
    "on-resistance (~80 ohm) varies with signal level, causing slight distortion; drive into high impedance to minimize it",
    "control input is a CMOS input; do not float it",
    "not zero-resistance and not infinite-off; charge injection clicks can appear when switching audio (mute during silence)"
